# Trivy ignore list — CVEs reviewed and accepted as non-exploitable in this
# deployment's actual architecture. See project report for full triage notes.
# Re-review each entry periodically in case an upstream fix becomes available.

# chromadb: pre-auth RCE requires a network-exposed chromadb server.
# This service uses chromadb.PersistentClient() (embedded mode) only —
# no HttpClient, no separate chromadb port/service. Not reachable.
CVE-2026-45829

# glib: D-Bus introspection XML parsing. Not invoked by this Python/FastAPI service.
CVE-2026-58016

# libxml2 (AI service base image): no XML parsing in this codebase
# (confirmed: no lxml or XML libraries in requirements.txt).
CVE-2026-6653

# perl / perl-base / Storable / perl-archive-tar: base Debian image includes
# Perl by default; this service never invokes it (Python-only application).
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-9538

# gzip: buffer overflow in gzip's legacy LZH decompression path. This
# service never shells out to gzip or decompresses untrusted .lzh/.lha
# input; Python's own gzip module (used for standard .gz handling, if any)
# is a separate implementation unaffected by this CVE.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1: symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl (get/setfacl)
# functions. This service never reads or modifies filesystem ACLs.
CVE-2026-54369

# glib (libglib2.0-0t64): same reasoning as CVE-2026-58016 above - present
# only as an opencv-python/libgl1 transitive dependency. This service never
# touches GVariant, GDateTime, GRegex, GIOChannel, GKeyFile, or GDBus APIs,
# so these internal-glib-parsing bugs have no reachable code path here.
CVE-2026-58010
CVE-2026-58011
CVE-2026-58012
CVE-2026-58013
CVE-2026-58014
CVE-2026-58015

# ncurses (libncursesw6/libtinfo6/ncurses-base/ncurses-bin): terminal
# rendering buffer overflow. This service runs headless behind uvicorn with
# no interactive TTY/PTY session, so no attacker-controlled input ever
# reaches ncurses's escape-sequence handling.
CVE-2025-69720

# util-linux/libblkid family (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2,
# libsmartcols1, libuuid1, util-linux): Debian's stable-security repo has
# shipped a fix (2.41.5-0+deb13u1) that Trivy's DB hadn't caught up to
# reporting as fixed as of this writing. Dockerfile now runs `apt-get
# upgrade` in the runtime stage to pull it in - keep this entry only as a
# fallback in case a rebuild briefly lags the mirror; remove once confirmed
# clean across builds.
CVE-2026-53615

# openssl / libssl3t64 / openssl-provider-legacy: DoS via unbounded memory
# growth in OpenSSL's native QUIC *server* (Listener) implementation, which
# only triggers when an app accepts inbound QUIC connections through
# OpenSSL's own SSL_accept()-based QUIC API. No fix is available yet
# upstream/in Debian as of this writing (Trivy status: fix_deferred).
# This service only ever speaks plain HTTP/TCP via uvicorn - confirmed no
# QUIC-capable package (aioquic, qh3, etc.) is installed anywhere in the
# image - so the vulnerable code path is never reached. Re-review once
# Debian ships a fixed openssl package.
CVE-2026-14456

# msgpack / setuptools: not our project's dependencies (those are pinned to
# fixed versions - msgpack 1.2.1, setuptools 78.1.1+ - in requirements.txt).
# These findings are pip's own internal vendored copies, declared in
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt and used only as pip._vendor.msgpack/setuptools
# for pip's own resolver - never imported or reachable by this service's code.
# Confirmed present at the same pinned versions in pip 26.2.1, the latest
# release as of this writing; will only change when pip ships a new bundle.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273